.Dd September 16, 2026
.Dt NDI_SET_ACC_FAULT 9F
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ndi_set_acc_fault ,
.Nm ndi_clr_acc_fault ,
.Nm ndi_set_dma_fault ,
.Nm ndi_clr_dma_fault
.Nd set and clear nexus handle fault indications
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/sunndi.h
.Ft "void"
.Fo ndi_set_acc_fault
.Fa "ddi_acc_handle_t ah"
.Fc
.Ft "void"
.Fo ndi_clr_acc_fault
.Fa "ddi_acc_handle_t ah"
.Fc
.Ft "void"
.Fo ndi_set_dma_fault
.Fa "ddi_dma_handle_t dh"
.Fc
.Ft "void"
.Fo ndi_clr_dma_fault
.Fa "ddi_dma_handle_t dh"
.Fc
.Sh INTERFACE LEVEL
illumos specific
.Pq Consolidation Private .
.Sh PARAMETERS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Va ah
Valid access handle managed by the nexus.
.It Va dh
Valid DMA handle managed by the nexus.
.El
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Nexus drivers use these functions to maintain fault indications on access
and DMA handles.
\fBndi_set_acc_fault()\fP marks an access handle faulty and
\fBndi_clr_acc_fault()\fP clears that indication.
\fBndi_set_dma_fault()\fP and \fBndi_clr_dma_fault()\fP perform the corresponding
operation on a DMA handle.
.Pp
A transition invokes the handle's fault-notification hook, when provided.
Repeating a set on an already faulty handle, or a clear on an already clear
handle, does not generate another transition notification.
The default handle-checking paths used by \fBddi_check_acc_handle()\fP and
\fBddi_check_dma_handle()\fP inspect these indications.
.Pp
Clearing an indication does not repair hardware or restore the contents of
memory affected by a DMA fault.
The nexus must coordinate recovery, synchronization, and the handle's
lifetime.
These functions do not acquire a lock around the fault transition and are
not replacements for the separate FMA error-state interfaces.
.Sh CONTEXT
These functions may be called in contexts supported by the nexus
fault-notification hook and its synchronization protocol.
They perform no memory allocation; any installed hook runs synchronously in
the caller's context.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
These functions have no return value.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ddi_check_acc_handle 9F ,
.Xr ddi_check_dma_handle 9F ,
.Xr ddi_fm_acc_err_get 9F ,
.Xr ddi_fm_dma_err_get 9F ,
.Xr sunndi 9F
